From 32fe188ed62581b5f7e4ba09ee832696e39ea968 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:53:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Route bare namespace calls and plaintext subagent tasks
 across providers

Live verification of 0014 showed Meta answers namespace calls in
two flattened shapes: sometimes the dotted name, sometimes the
bare child name with no namespace at all ("wait_agent"). Codex
rejects the bare form as an unsupported call. Qualify a bare call
to its dotted descriptor key when exactly one declared namespace
child carries that name, so the shared restorer can split it on
every response path; converted custom tools are recognized in the
bare form too.

The same live run exposed the mirror problem on the child side: a
task spawned by a non-OpenAI parent reaches a Codex-provider child
as plaintext inside an agent_message encrypted_content part, and
the Codex backend rejects the turn trying to decrypt the
plaintext ("Encrypted function output content could not be
decrypted or decoded"). Surface non-Fernet carriers as input_text
in the Codex executor, keeping genuine OpenAI Fernet payloads
opaque for the backend to decrypt.
